input.content:
Generate 1 sabotage suggestion for an polymorphism task in javascript.

Language syntax reference:
JavaScript OOP:
- Class: class Animal { constructor(name) { this.name = name; } speak() { return this.name; } }
- Inheritance: class Dog extends Animal { constructor(name) { super(name); } }
- Private: use #field syntax or closures. Use #balance for private fields.
- Polymorphism: override methods in subclass, no keyword needed

Task prompt: Your task is to implement polymorphism for a set of magical items. You need to extend the base `MagicItem` class and override its `activate()` method in two subclasses: `HealingElixir` and `FireballScroll` to provide unique behaviors.

Current code in the editor:
```
class MagicItem {
  constructor(name) {
    this.name = name;
  }

  activate() {
    // TODO: Implement a generic activation message or throw an error if not overridden
    return `${this.name} performs a generic action.`;
  }
}

class HealingElixir extends MagicItem {
  constructor(name, healAmount) {
    super(name);
    this.healAmount = healAmount;
  }

  activate() {
    // TODO: Override this method to return a specific healing message
    // Example: "The Potent Elixir heals for 50 health!"
  }
}

class FireballScroll extends MagicItem {
  constructor(name, damageAmount) {
    super(name);
    this.damageAmount = damageAmount;
  }

  activate() {
    // TODO: Override this method to return a specific damage message
    // Example: "The Scroll of Inferno unleashes a fireball dealing 75 damage!"
  }
}

// Test cases (for player to see expected output)
const elixir = new HealingElixir("Potent Elixir", 50);
const scroll = new FireballScroll("Scroll of Inferno", 75);

console.log(elixir.activate());
console.log(scroll.activate());
```

